\section{Introduction}
Sempan is spoken by the Sempan people in Mimika Regency, Central Papua, Indonesia. It is classified in the Asmat--Kamoro group. Speaker numbers of about 1,000 are cited from 1975 and 1987 figures. The search found very little for Sempan. It is described in sources as attested essentially through the work of the missionary linguist Drabbe. This report is therefore short.

\section{Primary Educational Resources}
None were found. No primer, textbook or school programme for Sempan appeared in the search results.

\section{Linguistic and Reference Materials}
\begin{itemize}
\item Wikipedia, ``Sempan language''. \url{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sempan_language}
\item Wikipedia, ``Sempan people''. \url{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sempan_people}
\item New Guinea World (University of Zurich), Sempan entry. It lists references, including a Drabbe dictionary marked as not obtained. \url{https://newguineaworld.linguistik.uzh.ch/families/trans-new-guinea/asmat-muli-strait/asmat-kamrau-bay/asmat-kamoro/sempan}
